    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0366" n="316" xml:id="pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.85/42</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Division of Operations of the United States
                        Shipping Board Emergency Fleet Corporation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steele</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Assistant of the Counselor for the Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Auchincloss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 17.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: We beg to hand you herewith copy of
                    memorandum under date of August 9 addressed to Mr. Munson
                    of the War Trade Board, also copy of cable from the Governor General of the
                    Philippine Islands which only reached us August 15.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d478-f1"/> You will note the Governor General of the Philippine
                    Islands requests that necessary steps be taken with the Japanese Ambassador to
                    have vessel [<hi rendition="#italic">Simferopol</hi>] return to Manila with coal
                    where legal proceedings may determine questions involved.</p>
                <p>We are passing this matter on to you, and will appreciate your taking it up with
                    the Japanese Ambassador along the above lines, at the same time keeping us
                    advised.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>Division of Operations <lb/> By <signed><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Semmes Steele</hi></signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d478-a1.xml" xpointer="d478-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
